 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Hair Type Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a hair type quiz?\", \"a\": \"A hair type quiz is a short set of questions about how your hair dries and curls, scored into one hair type. Hair comes in four main types: straight, wavy, curly, and coily. The quiz on this page uses those four and ends each result with a care routine.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a hair type quiz?\", \"a\": \"Describe the results and the business behind them, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> writes the questions and the table that stores each result. Ask for a product list or an email field on the result screen with a follow-up prompt, then publish the quiz link.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a curly hair type quiz split Curly into letter subtypes?\", \"a\": \"Only if your advice changes between them. The four types are broken down into subtypes A, B, and C based on texture, thickness, and curl pattern. If a 3A and a 3C visitor would get the same products, keep one Curly result and add a follow-up question on curl size.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I offer a hair type quiz free to every visitor on my site?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Charge nothing to take it, and use the result to point visitors to products or a booking. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing the quiz. A brand that also sells clothing can run a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a> on the same site.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a hair types quiz have?\", \"a\": \"Eight questions are enough to separate four results. Give each question one screen and one option per result. Stop at ten, and cut any question whose answers never change a result.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a what's my hair type quiz decide the result?\", \"a\": \"It counts answers. Each option points to one result, and the result with the most points wins. In the quiz above, a tie goes to the result listed first. On Emergent, every answer sits beside its result in a database you own, so you can see which question decided a close call.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a hair type quiz for female customers need different questions?\", \"a\": \"No. The questions are about the hair itself: how it dries and holds a curl. Ask about length or styling habits only if your results change with them. Write every option in plain words, because the quiz should never read like a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a> on terms such as porosity.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a quiz for hair type recommend products from my store?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Tag each product with the hair types it suits, and the app lists the matching ones on each result screen. If your catalog lives on another store platform, an app built on Emergent can connect to it through its API and read the tags from there.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a hair type quiz ask about porosity?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if your products differ by it. Porosity refers to how much moisture your hair absorbs and holds. Ask about it as something the visitor can see at home, show it as a separate line on the result, and test the wording on a few people before it changes any recommendation.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get more people to take my hair type quiz?\", \"a\": \"Put the quiz where hair decisions happen: on product pages, in the order confirmation, and on the booking page. If you sell a trial-size kit, send each result to a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a> for that kit. Link the quiz from posts that show the four hair types side by side.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
